.TH ITCMDR\-ADMIN 1 "" "itcmdr" "itcmdr manual"
.SH NAME
itcmdr\-admin \- command line client for adminsvr
.SH ITCMDR\-ADMIN
.nf
itcmdr adminsvr CLI (same signed API as the admin app)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-admin [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  help        The guides (docs/) in the terminal: `help` lists topics, `help <topic>` prints one
  info        adminsvr version and root key (unsigned)
  trust       v1.1.0: the certificate adminsvr presents and how this device trusts it
  enroll      Enroll this device with a one\-time code: shows your 24 words ONCE, then asks three back
  recover     New device from your 24 words (read from stdin): restore the backed\-up key or certify a new one
  whoami      
  user        
  device      
  key\-backup  
  site        
  alert       
  backup      
  command     
  audit       
  passkey     Passkeys / security keys: the optional second factor (needs libfido2's tools)
  policy      Which actions need a passkey touch, and for which roles a passkey is required (owners set it)
  push        Push notifications for alerts on this device (FCM / APNs token; the admin app does this itself)
  org         Org\-wide settings: whether every approval needs a second owner/admin (owners set it)
  release     Server/agent releases: approve one once, then roll it out to sites (v0.21.0)
  config      A site's settings and schedules as adminsvr sees them; set a setting (v0.20.0)
  schedule    Run, pause or resume a site's schedule (by the id from `config show`)
  plugin      Plugin catalog, a site's plugins, enable/disable/push (two\-person)
  freeze      Global freeze of every command (owners)
\&
Options:
      \-\-home <HOME>
          Where this device's identity lives (default: the user config dir; env ITCMDR_ADMIN_HOME)
      \-\-trust\-fingerprint <TRUST_FINGERPRINT>
          v1.1.0: trust adminsvr's certificate when it is not trusted by this system (self\-signed or private CA): only this exact SHA\-256 is accepted, and it is remembered for this server
      \-\-trust\-anyway
          Also accept that certificate when it is expired or does not match the name (explicit override)
  \-h, \-\-help
          Print help
  \-V, \-\-version
          Print version
.fi
